{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Gad has come.</b> This one came by chance, for my intention was not to bring this one into the world, had I not ceased bearing. And it is written בגד as one word, for the pregnancy was to her a בוגד (boged, traitor) like a deception — the pregnancy having ceased from her after it had begun, as in the verse: אַחַי בָּגְדוּ כְמוֹ נָחַל (Job 6:15)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The wordplay turns on the name גד (Gad) read together with the letters ב (bet) preceding it in בגד, yielding בגד — both 'troop/fortune' and the root בגד ('deceit/betrayal'). Sforno reads Leah as saying the pregnancy 'deceived' her by appearing to resume then being cut short; hence the full form בגד encodes both the name and the betrayal."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:28.908062055Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}